# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise of the entangling layers with `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Pelajari noise dari layer entangling dengan `qiskit-noise-learning` {#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. We assume a Markovian noise model, and therefore only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned, because the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the amplification will be.\n"
msgstr "PEA diawali dengan mempelajari model noise twirled dari setiap layer gate entangling di dalam circuit. Kita mengasumsikan model noise Markovian, sehingga hanya model noise dari setiap layer gate entangling yang unik yang perlu dipelajari, karena kedalaman circuit diasumsikan tidak memengaruhi kanal noise dari suatu layer entangling. Makin akurat model noise yang dipelajari, makin akurat pula amplifikasinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use `qiskit-noise-learning` for learning the noise. The learner repeats each layer `fragment_depths` times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit `num_randomizations` times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. The following code draws the learned noise model, with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y, and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates; a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr "Kita memakai `qiskit-noise-learning` untuk mempelajari noise. Learner mengulang setiap layer sebanyak `fragment_depths` kali di dalam circuit pembelajarannya, men-twirl setiap circuit sebanyak `num_randomizations` kali, lalu mencocokkan peluruhan fidelity hasil pengukuran ke model Pauli-Lindblad. Kode berikut menggambar model noise yang dipelajari, dengan kedua layer digabung menjadi satu peta. Setiap qubit berupa diagram pie dari laju X, Y, dan Z berbobot-1 yang dijumlahkan pada kedua layer, dan setiap edge menunjukkan laju berbobot-2 yang dipelajari; laju ``3e-4`` berarti error itu terjadi kira-kira tiga dari setiap 10.000 kali pemakaian layer.\n"

